  clock: 4  # fca9
  nonce: fca9  # fca9
  message: "WONT_DO: the stated premise (receiver None on 100% of edges = unpopulated field) is a single-language-corpus artifact, not a defect. Behavioral evidence: analysing a Ruby file emits edge.meta.receiver=constant_external on a SomeModule.run call (ruby.py:2293). receiver is a fold-residue key (audit-findings 0012) emitted only by ruby/go/csharp/rust/cpp; hypergumbo's own Python/JS tree exercises none of them, and the dominant Python method-call fold omits receiver BY DESIGN (audit-findings 0012 addendum line 335). ADR-0040 classifies this as the evidence_lang shape (real producers, 0-on-self-corpus) -> keep, not populate/deprecate. Real minor issue surfaced + fixed in PR #579: stale documented vocabulary (spec said bare/external/typed; producers emit bare/external/stdlib/generic/constant_external/field_chain/typed_field/typed_var) -> spec 841 + MetaKeySpec now accurate. WI-lodaz already folded here as duplicate. Optional follow-up (R2): normalize/enumerate the 8-value producer vocabulary across the 5 emitters."  # fca9
